    "lawCode": "Amd §343-a, add §344-n, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7620A\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating portions of\nthe state highway system as \"The Disabled American Veterans - New York\nMedal of Honor Highway\", the \"New York Medal of Honor Highway\" and the\n\"Sergeant Jonathan Gollnitz - New York Medal of Honor Highway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to designate route 20 as the \"New York Medal\nof Honor Highway\", while preserving other designations.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. amends section 343-a of the highway law to designate route 20\nas the \"New York Medal of Honor Highway\".\n\nSection 2. amends section 344-n of the highway law to provide further\nchanges for the disgnation of route 20 as the \"New York Medal of Honor\nHighway\".\n\nSection 3. amends section 344-h of the highway law to provide provide\nfurther changes for the disgnation of route 20 as the \"New York Medal of\nHonor Highway\".\n\nSection 4. provides for proper signage pursuant to this act. Section\n\n4. is the enacting clause\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is part of a country wide effort to designate U.S. Highway 20\nas \"The Medal of Honor Highway\". At 3,365 miles in length, U.S.  Highway\n20 is the longest highway in our nation. Its western terminus is in\nNewport, OR on the Pacific Ocean, crosses 12 states with its eastern\nterminus in Boston, MA at the Atlantic Ocean.\n\nAbout 2,360 recipients or two-thirds (67%) of all 3,508 Medal of Honor\nawards presented since 1863 are connected with the 12 states: Oregon,\nIdaho, Montana, Wyoming, Nebraska, Iowa, Illinois, Indiana, Ohio, Penn-\nsylvania, New York and Massachusetts. Twenty-six (26) of our nation's 67\nliving recipients are also connected with U.S. Hwy 20 in those states.\n\nLegislatures and Governors in Oregon, Idaho, Montana, Wyoming, Nebraska,\nIowa, Indiana and Pennsylvania have already designated state Medal of\nHonor Highway covering 68% of the 3,365 mile Medal of Honor Highway\nAcross America between the Pacific and Atlantic Oceans.\n\nSeventy two (72) signs have already been installed in those states.\n\nThis bill will help complete the nationwide effort to designate U.S.\nHighway 20 as \"The Medal of Honor Highway\".\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
